{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You came in with nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea—can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been vomiting several times a day for about five days and have had diarrhea with undigested food. My stomach pain has gotten worse too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Given your history of fibrosing mesenteritis and multiple bowel obstructions, we’re concerned this could be another partial small bowel obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds familiar. I’ve had this before. Does that mean I can’t eat again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, we’ll keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—to let your bowel rest. We’ll give you fluids and nutrition through your G-tube and IV for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My G-tube has been draining a lot lately. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re keeping it on suction to help decompress your stomach. It’s been draining 500 to 1200 mL daily, which makes sense with the obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin? I take it for blood clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was 2.0 on admission—within the therapeutic range. We’ll keep monitoring it and adjust your warfarin dose as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want another bleed like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2183-04-06 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be careful. For now, we’re continuing your home dose of 2.5 mg daily and will adjust based on labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we reviewed your abdominal X-ray from yesterday. It shows a normal bowel gas pattern—no signs of complete obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not fully blocked? That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s still a partial obstruction, which is why we’re keeping you NPO and on G-tube suction for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long will I need to stay like this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It depends on how quickly your bowel recovers. We’ll monitor your symptoms and output. It could be several days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2183-04-08 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting you on total parenteral nutrition—TPN—through your port-a-cath since you haven’t been able to eat for over a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2183-04-08 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember TPN from last time. Will I need it at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2183-04-08 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re arranging for home TPN. You’ll continue it until your GI doctor clears you to restart oral intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2183-04-08 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I hope it doesn’t take too long."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2183-04-09 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain team reviewed your meds. We’re increasing your MS Contin to 30 mg twice daily for better pain control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2183-04-09 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling more drowsy. Is that from the morphine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2183-04-09 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll monitor you closely. If the drowsiness continues, we may need to reduce the dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2183-04-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been more somnolent the past day. We’re reducing your MS Contin back to 15 mg twice daily—the dose you were on at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2183-04-10 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt too out of it. I’m glad we’re adjusting it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2183-04-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also reduced your promethazine to three times a day. It can add to drowsiness, especially with narcotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2183-04-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ll stick to that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2183-04-11 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been low in the mornings—around 90s/60s—but you’re not symptomatic. We’re encouraging more fluids by mouth when you can tolerate them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2183-04-11 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do feel a bit weak when I stand. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2183-04-11 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "As long as you’re not dizzy or passing out, it’s okay. We’ll keep an eye on it. Staying hydrated will help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2183-04-12 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We started your TPN yesterday. It’s going well—no complications so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2183-04-12 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’m glad something is helping me get nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2183-04-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was 2.4 today. We’re increasing your warfarin to 5 mg daily to keep it in the therapeutic range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2183-04-13 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with the TPN and everything else?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2183-04-13 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re monitoring closely. Your labs are stable, and you’re not bleeding. It’s important to stay anticoagulated due to your DVT history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2183-04-14 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your G-tube is showing signs of granulation tissue. We’ve scheduled a procedure with interventional radiology to replace it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2183-04-14 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that urgent? I’m already feeling weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2183-04-14 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not an emergency, but replacing it now prevents complications later. The procedure is quick and done under local anesthesia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2183-04-14 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2183-04-15 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The G-tube was successfully replaced today under CT guidance. It’s now functioning well and ready for use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2183-04-15 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Did it go okay? I felt some pressure but not much pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2183-04-15 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it went smoothly. They cauterized some granulation tissue, and the new tube is secure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2183-04-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest X-ray shows no bowel obstruction. Your G-tube output has decreased to about 800 mL yesterday, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2183-04-16 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean I might start eating soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2183-04-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not there yet, but it’s moving in the right direction. We’ll keep monitoring and discuss with your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2183-04-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.2—perfect. We’ll keep your warfarin at 5 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2183-04-17 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ll need to follow up with my PCP for checks, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2183-04-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please schedule regular INR checks with your primary care or anticoagulation clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2183-04-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is much better, and you’re more alert. We’re switching your pain meds back to your home regimen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2183-04-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel more like myself. Can I start trying liquids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2183-04-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll talk to GI about it. For now, we’re focusing on stabilizing your nutrition with TPN at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2183-04-19 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture came back with low bacterial count—less than 10,000 organisms/mL. No infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2183-04-19 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought I might have a UTI. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2183-04-19 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, no antibiotics needed. Your symptoms are from the bowel issue, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2183-04-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Another X-ray today shows no obstruction. Your bowel is recovering. We’re planning for discharge in the next day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2183-04-20 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news! What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2183-04-20 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue TPN at home, monitor your G-tube output, and follow up with your GI doctor about restarting food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2183-04-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve updated your discharge meds. Warfarin is now 5 mg daily, and your short-acting morphine is available for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2183-04-21 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the promethazine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2183-04-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it no more than three times a day. We want to avoid drowsiness, especially with your other meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2183-04-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re discharging you home with home health support for TPN."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2183-04-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll follow up with my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2183-04-22 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please keep your appointments. Call us if you have increasing pain, vomiting, or signs of infection at the G-tube site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2183-04-22 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m ready to get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2183-04-22 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2183-04-06 16:06:00",
    "admission_end": "2183-04-22 12:28:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with a complex history including fibrosing mesenteritis, recurrent small bowel obstruction, and G-tube dependence, was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea concerning for partial small bowel obstruction. She was managed conservatively with NPO status, G-tube suction, and pain control. Due to prolonged inability to eat, TPN was initiated and arranged for home continuation. Her G-tube was replaced due to granulation tissue, and her warfarin dose was adjusted to 5 mg daily with a therapeutic INR at discharge. She experienced somnolence from increased narcotics and antiemetics, prompting a return to her baseline medication regimen. Her condition improved, and she was discharged home with home health services for TPN and close outpatient follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Gastrostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
